From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:01:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] webservices: HTTP listener and reply channel on a local
 socket

WsCreateListener accepts WS_CHANNEL_TYPE_REPLY over WS_HTTP_CHANNEL_BINDING
instead of failing with E_NOTIMPL. WsOpenListener binds the host and port of an
http:// URL (host wildcards + and * allowed), WsAcceptChannel waits for a POST
whose path lies under the registered path, reads it (Content-Length or chunked,
Expect: 100-continue answered) and returns an open channel holding the request.
Other requests get 404, 405, 411 or 413 and the wait continues. WsReceiveMessage
and WsReadMessageStart read the request, WsSendReplyMessage answers with 200, or
500 for a fault message, and Connection: close. https:// is E_NOTIMPL.

